 "title": "Advanced animation 1: F-curves and the graph editor",
 "summary": "The graph editor on one move (keys at frames 1, 100 and 200: along Y and back) given to six cubes in lanes so the F-curves can be compared: Bezier as Blender makes it (slow-fast-slow), Linear (constant speed), Sinusoidal, Bezier handles dragged by hand (a long flat start, a steep fast arrival, the way back linear), a Noise modifier on the X location so one vibrates as it goes, and (beyond the tutorial) Bounce easing; every Y curve made cyclic so the move repeats.",
